From 4b24631c6ebfb8e42c592fb56abbf707ab5a0d27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:16:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): kanban drawer: a kind whose reads keep failing
 stops sending foreground refetches [daveey]

Follow-up to PR #2102 (review 5889787422, non-blocking points 1-2).

1. Unbounded foreground on failing reads. userOpenReads counted a kind as delivered only after a successful read, so
   when every read failed (gateway unreachable, task gone, timeouts on a very slow link) each interval refetch of
   that open stayed priority 'foreground': the task every 30 s, the log every 3-15 s, all bypassing the slow-link
   thinner and the power-settle hold. The open read of a kind now settles when a read answers OR when a fetch whose
   reads all failed has spent React Query's retries. The query function passes `retryingFetch(context)`: React
   Query counts a fetch's failures (fetchFailureCount) before each retry and resets the count when a new fetch
   starts, so a retry keeps the foreground tag while the next fetch after a failed one is a background poll.
   Per-open state, so a re-open of a task whose cached query is in error is still the user's foreground read.
2. Interval comment. The warm-cache test comment said "15-30 s later"; the drawer said "3-30 s". The test covers the
   task query (30 s): the test now says "the task query's interval refetch 30 s later" and the drawer comment
   spells out "3-30 s later (log 3-15 s, task 30 s)".

Test (fails before, passes after), drawer.test.tsx:
- "makes the refetches of a kind whose reads all fail polls once its first fetch spent its retries"
  (retry: 1; before: ['foreground','foreground','foreground','foreground'], after:
  ['foreground','foreground',undefined,undefined]: the retried first read stays foreground).
Kanban plugin vitest 145/145, tsc --noEmit clean, eslint clean on the touched files.
